        "question": "What is the deadline and late payment penalty for stamping a Sale and Purchase Agreement in Singapore?",
        "answer": "Stamp duty must be paid within 14 days of contract signing in Singapore (or 30 days if executed overseas). Under Section 46 of the Stamp Duties Act, late payments incur penalties up to S$25 or the duty owed (if under 3 months), and up to 4 times the duty owed if delayed beyond 3 months."
